  "notes": "כרטיסים.נט (kartisim.net) — Israeli show guide (Laravel + Livewire) that redirects to the Cartis/Kartisim box office (/go/event-date/<id> → net.kartisim.co.il/announce/buy/…). Section pages (/section/<x>, sorted by nearest performance, 12 shows per page, server-side ?page=N) → entry.follow every /event/<slug> show page (regex excludes the per-date /event/<slug>/<id> pages) → one row per performance from the schedule table (tr[onclick*='/go/event-date/']: date dd/mm/yyyy, time, hall, street, Hebrew city → city_aliases); name / og:image / EventSeries description are page_fields. purchase_link = the kartisim redirect (outbound to the seller), source_id = the event-date id (same id the per-date JSON-LD page uses). 11 sections × 3 pages ≤ 300 followed show pages ≈ 330 requests / run at 48 h; the sitemap lists 5,167 show pages, so the horizon is the nearest few weeks per section. No performer markup → artist_name empty. Same back-end as youticket / firstline / kupatbravo → expect the weekly (venue,date,name≈) dedup to merge overlaps. Dry run 2026-09-20 (3 sections × 1 page → 36 show pages): 42 performances (~1.2 per show page), venue/city/time 100 %, no prices on the schedule table; 21/42 already in prod (bravo 14, mevalim 9)."
